                "text": "Use the antiderivative $\\int e^{-st}\\,dt=-\\frac{1}{s}e^{-st}$. At the lower bound, $\\left.-\\frac{1}{s}e^{-st}\\right|_{t\\to0^-}= -\\frac{1}{s}\\cdot 1$. At the upper bound, $\\lim_{b\\to\\infty}(-\\frac{1}{s}e^{-sb})=0$ only when $\\operatorname{Re}(s)>0$, leaving $\\frac{1}{s}$.",
                "latex": "",
                "image_slot_id": ""
              }
            ]
